        <groundspeak:log id="249333525">
          <groundspeak:log_wpt lat="56.216400" lon="-117.274350" />
          <groundspeak:date>2012-07-11T20:00:00</groundspeak:date>
          <groundspeak:type>Found it</groundspeak:type>
          <groundspeak:finder id="985002">Strider&#39;s Ride</groundspeak:finder>
          <groundspeak:text encoded="True">&lt;p&gt;BCP565 Judah Hill&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Of all the caps I've ever visited, this one has to rank right up there in the top 10. The views overlooking the valley, the Peace River and the bridge are simply spectacular, combined with the big blue skies and terrific weather made this one memorable. After finding the cap, we carried on up the road a bit to a spot where there's a park and viewpoint.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;TFTCap ofth&lt;/p&gt;

          </groundspeak:text>
        </groundspeak:log>
        <groundspeak:log id="248786677">
          <groundspeak:log_wpt lat="56.216350" lon="-117.274333" />
          <groundspeak:date>2012-07-11T20:00:00</groundspeak:date>
          <groundspeak:type>Found it</groundspeak:type>
          <groundspeak:finder id="321730">Sleepy_hollow</groundspeak:finder>
          <groundspeak:text encoded="True">&lt;p&gt;BCP565 - Judah Hill&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Well I've been through Peace River several times and have never visited Judah Hill - what a terrific viewpoint! It took us a little time to find the correct access, but once we did it was only a short walk to the cap site at this well chosen location - TFTH and fun!&lt;/p&gt;

          </groundspeak:text>
        </groundspeak:log>
        <groundspeak:log id="247965958">
          <groundspeak:date>2012-07-08T20:00:00</groundspeak:date>
          <groundspeak:type>Found it</groundspeak:type>
          <groundspeak:finder id="1565005">Takin it Easy</groundspeak:finder>
          <groundspeak:text encoded="True">&lt;p&gt;BCP565 Judah Hill

Posted: N56° 12.981 W117° 16.460

GPSr: N56° 12.982 W117° 16.459&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Our last stop of the day.  After dinner we went for a drive up the hill to look down at the valley prior to dusk.  What a beautiful spot.  A great place for a published cap.  Thanks for setting this one up OFTH.  We stayed awhile and enjoyed the view.&lt;/p&gt;

          </groundspeak:text>
        </groundspeak:log>
